#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:2
msgid "AI Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:4
msgid "|advanced-plus|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:6
msgid ""
"HPE Morpheus Enterprise includes an integrated AI assistant that helps "
"operators manage infrastructure through natural language. The AI Services"
" feature connects large language models (LLMs) to Morpheus capabilities "
"via the Model Context Protocol (MCP), enabling conversational access to "
"provisioning, monitoring, reporting, and infrastructure management."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:8
msgid "AI Services is accessed from |TooAI| and consists of three components:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:10
msgid ""
"**AI Agents** — Configure the AI assistant's behavior, model selection, "
"and tool access"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:11
msgid ""
"**MCP Servers** — Connect external tool providers that extend the AI's "
"capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:12
msgid "**LLM Integrations** — View connected language model providers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:26
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:28
msgid "The AI assistant uses a layered architecture:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Users interact** with the AI chat assistant — a chat interface "
"available to authenticated users"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:31
msgid ""
"**AI Agents** receive messages and route them to a configured **LLM** "
"(language model)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:32
msgid ""
"The LLM can invoke **tools** exposed by MCP Servers to query or act on "
"Morpheus resources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:33
msgid "**Responses** are returned with context from the tools used"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:35
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:37
msgid ""
"The built-in Morpheus MCP server provides tools for common operations "
"(listing instances, checking cloud status, querying reports, etc.) "
"without any external configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:40
msgid "Security & Permissions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:42
msgid "AI Services access is controlled by two role permissions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:48
msgid "Permission"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:49
msgid "Access Levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:50
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:51
msgid "**AI Services** (``services-ai``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:52 ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:55
msgid "None, Read, Full"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:53
msgid ""
"Controls access to |TooAI| configuration. Read = view only; Full = "
"create/edit/delete agents, MCP servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:54
msgid "**AI Agentic Tools** (``services-ai-agentic``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:56
msgid ""
"Controls tool execution. Read = AI can only use read-only/GET tools; Full"
" = AI can execute write/modify operations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:58
msgid ""
"Additionally, individual AI Agents can be configured with **Read-Only "
"Tools** mode, which restricts that agent to non-destructive operations "
"regardless of the user's permission level."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tools/ai/ai.rst:60
msgid ""
"Tool operations that modify resources (create, delete, reconfigure) "
"require **user confirmation** before execution, providing a safety "
"mechanism against unintended changes."
msgstr ""

